
%% DOCK
#dam-base
(room *)
(name *)	Dam Base
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are at the base of Flood Control Dam \#3, which looms above you and
	to the north. The river Frigid is flowing by here. Across the river are
	the White Cliffs which seem to form a giant wall stretching from north
	to south along the east shore of the river as it winds its way
	downstream.
(from * go #north to #dam-room)
(from * go #up to #dam-room)
(from * go #launch to #frigid-river1)

%% RIVR1
#frigid-river1
(room *)
(name *)	Frigid River
(inherently dark *)
(* is water)
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are on the River Frigid in the vicinity of the Dam. The river flows
	quietly here. There is a landing on the west shore.
(narrate failing to leave * #up)
	You cannot go upstream due to strong currents.
(from * go #west to #dam-base)
(from * go #land to #dam-base)
(from * go #down to #frigid-river2)
(narrate failing to leave * #east)
	The White Cliffs prevent your landing here.

%% RIVR2
#frigid-river2
(room *)
(name *)	Frigid River
(inherently dark *)
(* is water)
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	The River turns a corner here making it impossible to see the Dam. The
	White Cliffs loom on the east bank and large rocks prevent landing on
	the west.
(narrate failing to leave * #up)
	You cannot go upstream due to strong currents.
(from * go #down to #frigid-river3)
(narrate failing to leave * #east)
	The White Cliffs prevent your landing here.

%% RIVR3
#frigid-river3
(room *)
(name *)	Frigid River
(inherently dark *)
(* is water)
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	The river descends here into a valley. There is a narrow beach on the
	east below the cliffs and there is some shore on the west which may be
	suitable. In the distance a faint rumbling can be heard.
(narrate failing to leave * #up)
	You cannot go upstream due to strong currents.
(from * go #down to #frigid-river4)
(from * go #east to #white-cliffs-beach1)
(from * go #west to #rocky-shore)
(narrate failing to leave * #land)
	You must specify which direction here.

%% WCLF1
#white-cliffs-beach1
(room *)
(name *)	White Cliffs Beach
(inherently dark *)
(* can be filled)
(look *)
	You are on a narrow strip of beach which runs along the base of the
	White Cliffs. The only path here is a narrow one, heading south along
	the Cliffs.
%% TODO: room action routine CLIFF-FUNCTION
(from * go #south to #white-cliffs-beach2)
%% TODO: conditional on flag DEFLATE
(prevent [from * go #south])
	~(deflate)
		The path is too narrow.
(from * go #launch to #frigid-river3)

%% WCLF2
#white-cliffs-beach2
(room *)
(name *)	White Cliffs Beach
(inherently dark *)
(* can be filled)
(look *)
	You are on a rocky, narrow strip of beach beside the Cliffs. A narrow
	path leads north along the shore.
%% TODO: room action routine CLIFF-FUNCTION
(from * go #north to #white-cliffs-beach1)
%% TODO: conditional on flag DEFLATE
(prevent [from * go #north])
	~(deflate)
		The path is too narrow.
(from * go #launch to #frigid-river4)

%% RIVR4
#frigid-river4
(room *)
(name *)	Frigid River
(inherently dark *)
(* is water)
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	The river is running faster here and the sound ahead appears to be that
	of rushing water. On the west shore is a sandy beach. A small area of
	beach can also be seen below the Cliffs.
%% TODO: room action routine RIVR4-ROOM
(narrate failing to leave * #up)
	You cannot go upstream due to strong currents.
(from * go #down to #frigid-river5)
(from * go #east to #white-cliffs-beach2)
(from * go #west to #sandy-beach)
(narrate failing to leave * #land)
	Specify the direction to land.

%% RIVR5
#frigid-river5
(room *)
(name *)	Frigid River
(inherently dark *)
(* is water)
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	The sound of rushing water is nearly unbearable here. On the west shore
	is a large landing area.
(from * go #land to #shore)
(narrate failing to leave * #down)
	(went over falls)

%% FANTE
#shore
(room *)
(name *)	Shore
(inherently dark *)
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are on the shore of the River. The river here seems somewhat
	treacherous. A path travels from north to south here, the south end
	quickly turning around a sharp corner.
(from * go #launch to #frigid-river5)
(from * go #north to #sandy-beach)
(from * go #south to #aragain-falls)

%% BEACH
#sandy-beach
(room *)
(name *)	Sandy Beach
(inherently dark *)
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are on a large sandy beach at the shore of the river, which is
	flowing quickly by. A path runs beside the river to the south here.
%% TODO: room action routine BEACH-ROOM
(from * go #launch to #frigid-river4)
(from * go #south to #shore)

%% RCAVE
#rocky-shore
(room *)
(name *)	Rocky Shore
(inherently dark *)
(* can be filled)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are on the west shore of the river. An entrance to a cave is to the
	northwest. The shore is very rocky here.
(from * go #launch to #frigid-river3)
(from * go #northwest to #small-cave)

%% TCAVE
#small-cave
(room *)
(name *)	Small Cave
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are in a small cave whose exits are on the south and northwest.
%% TODO: room action routine TCAVE-ROOM
(from * go #south to #rocky-shore)
(from * go #northwest to #ancient-chasm)

%% BARRE
#barrel
(room *)
(name *)	Barrel
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
	You are in a barrel. Congratulations. Etched into the side of the barrel
	is the word 'Geronimo!'.
(from * go #out to #aragain-falls)

%% FALLS
#aragain-falls
(room *)
(name *)	Aragain Falls
(inherently dark *)
(* is sacred)
(look *)
	You are at the top of Aragain Falls, an enormous waterfall with a
	drop of about 450 feet.  The only path here is on the north end.
	There is a man-sized barrel here which you could fit into.
	(if) (rainbow is solid) (then)
		A solid rainbow spans the falls.
	(else)
		A beautiful rainbow can be seen over the falls and to the east.
	(endif)
(notice #rainbow)
(from * go #north to #shore)
(from * go #in to #barrel)
(from * go #east/#up to #rainbow-room)
	(rainbow is solid)

(narrate failing to leave * #down)
	(went over falls)

(went over falls)
	Oh dear, you seem to have gone over Aragain Falls.  Not a very smart
	thing to do, apparently.
	(jigs up)
